I had an encounter with a shopkeeper recently which made me admire their
incredible properties even more. I was trying to shoplift a haul  of goodies
from a small general store, I had my pickaxe and had dug a pit ready to
break through the floor and make my escape  when I remembered the shopkeepers
habit of running over and grabbing my rucksack as I fall through the floor.
"I Know how to fix him" I thought, so I took my pick axe and dug pits in
/every/ space left in the shop. I went back to the far corner and dug through.
Imagine my surprise when the shopkeeper leapt accross the room, clearing
several pits, landed (presumably hovering?) on the pit beside mine and took
my rucksack.

Who trains these  guys?? Billy Smart?

Oh and how about (a small mod for next version) making objects fall through
holes in the floor, its a bit unrealistic to be able to chuck stuff onto a 
trapdoor and have it stay there. I'm sure shopkeepers could be made to spot
customers chucking goods through a hole in the floor and get angry about it 
if necessary.

< And could someone please email me the spoiler file, I can't use ftp >

David.

